                <pb facs="0673" n="549" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg549"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.1211/145: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-08-13T15:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 13,
                                1923—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:05
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>77. Your telegram number 110, August 12. From Warren: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“We have already informed the representatives of the Governments
                            mentioned that Department will advise them of results of the
                            negotiations. An agreement has been reached with the authorities here
                            that neither the minutes nor the proposed conventions shall be released
                            until we return and some concerted action is agreed to by both
                            Governments.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
